{"text":"There's a poem in Florida and East Texas where streets swell into a nexus of vivers, cows afloat like mottled buoys in the brown. What courage is now so common that 23-year-old Jesus Contreras rescues people from floodwaters. There's a poem in Los Angeles yawning while teaching a Pacific tide where a single mother swelters in a windowless classroom teaching black and brown students in Watts to spell out their thoughts so her daughter might write this poem for you. There's a lyric in California where thousands of students march for blocks undocumented and unafraid where my friend Rosa finds the power to blossom and deadlock her spirit the bedrock of her community. She knows hope is like a stubborn ship gripping a dock, a truth, that you can't stop a dreamer or knock down a dream. How could this not be her city su nation, our country, our America, or American lyric to write to?","words":[{"text":"There's","start":0.0,"end":0.56},{"text":"a","start":0.56,"end":0.64},{"text":"poem","start":0.64,"end":1.04},{"text":"in","start":1.04,"end":1.54},{"text":"Florida","start":1.54,"end":2.02},{"text":"and","start":2.02,"end":2.76},{"text":"East","start":2.76,"end":3.04},{"text":"Texas","start":3.04,"end":3.64},{"text":"where","start":3.64,"end":4.36},{"text":"streets","start":4.36,"end":4.74},{"text":"swell","start":4.74,"end":5.22},{"text":"into","start":5.22,"end":5.6},{"text":"a","start":5.6,"end":5.74},{"text":"nexus","start":5.74,"end":6.2},{"text":"of","start":6.2,"end":6.58},{"text":"vivers","start":6.58,"end":7.04,"punct":","},{"text":"cows","start":7.34,"end":7.54},{"text":"afloat","start":7.54,"end":8.0},{"text":"like","start":8.0,"end":8.36},{"text":"mottled","start":8.36,"end":9.16},{"text":"buoys","start":9.16,"end":9.74},{"text":"in","start":9.74,"end":10.14},{"text":"the","start":10.14,"end":10.28},{"text":"brown","start":10.28,"end":10.66,"punct":"."},{"text":"What","start":11.38,"end":11.46},{"text":"courage","start":11.46,"end":11.88},{"text":"is","s